cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CHECO26, please cite this database and the source products listed
  under `references`. Per-layer licensing differs: not every layer is
  redistributable under the same terms.
title: "CHECO26: A China-wide cross-thematic raster database at 1-km resolution for ecological research"
abstract: >-
  A uniform-grid library of 21,110 environmental layers covering China at 1 km in
  an equal-area Albers projection (WGS 84, central meridian 105 E, standard
  parallels 25 N and 47 N). Twenty-one dataset entries drawn from nineteen source
  products across eight categories (bioclim, soil, lulc, anthro, hydro, vege,
  dist, topo) are standardised to one grid of 4,861 x 4,062 cells, one data type
  (float32) and one NoData convention (-9999). Besides the harmonised source
  layers the database delivers 16,286 focal-statistics layers at four radii
  (1, 5, 10 and 20 km), 17 distance surfaces and per-cell areal proportions for
  every categorical source. Land use and land cover is provided at three
  complementary depths: annual observed cover 2000-2025 (CLCD, 1,170 layers), a
  China-relevant projection (GLU1km, 540 layers) and a harmonised yearly
  reconstruction 1960-2100 under five SSP-RCP scenarios (18,440 layers). Total
  volume is 169.4 GB.
version: "2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
